:: kavya_mirror_scene
<<img "kavya_wakeup.png" "Room 304, pre-dawn">>
The mirror on the cupboard door, clouded and rust-spotted, gives you back in fragments. Dusky skin. Dark circles from a night spent debugging a tokenizer module until 2 AM. The beauty mark below your left eye. Wavy black hair that fights every comb.

<<th "Kavya Iyer. Twenty-one. MBBS third year. Daughter of Dr. Venkatesh Iyer, orthopaedic surgeon. Future doctor. Present prisoner.">>

<<hubreturn>>


:: meera_observation
Meera is on the middle bed, spine against the wall, knees pulled up, reading in the dim light. Not a textbook   you know every textbook in this room by cover and thickness. This is something old. Palm leaves threaded together, brittle, the colour of old tea. Her lips move silently. Sanskrit   you recognise the mouth shapes.

"Kya padh rahi hai subah subah?"<span class="gloss-en">What are you reading so early in the morning?</span>

She startles. Presses it to her chest with both hands. "Kuch nahi. Library se mili. Sanskrit text."<span class="gloss-en">Nothing. Got it from the library. A Sanskrit text.</span> That smile   the one that means she's holding an ocean behind the dam of her lips. "Theek hoon."<span class="gloss-en">I'm fine.</span>

She's not theek. She hasn't been theek in six months. But Meera reveals on her own schedule, like a slow-release medication.

<<run setup.flag("noticed_manuscript")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: priya_status_check
<<if setup.has("priya_asks") or setup.clock() gte 780>>\
Priya drops onto her bed, opens Instagram   the recovery protocol   and pitches her voice half an octave higher. The favour-asking tone.

<div class="dialogue">"Kavya. Mujhe 'candid' photos chahiye. Campus mein. Like I'm walking and not looking at the camera and the light is catching my hair."<span class="gloss-en">Kavya. I need 'candid' photos. On campus.</span></div>

"You want me to photograph you pretending you don't know photos are being taken."

<div class="dialogue">"Exactly! You understand!"</div>

<<run setup.flag("priya_asks")>>
<<th "There's a real girl under the Instagram filter   lonely, wanting to feel pretty. You can't hate her for that. Only for the circumstances that put her between you and the people you're protecting.">>
<<hubreturn>>
<<else>>\
Priya's alarm   a Jawan song at construction-site volume   has been going for a minute forty. She rolls over, slaps the screen, opens one eye behind the glasses she slept in again.

<div class="dialogue">"Kavyaaa. Aaj ka day kya hai?"<span class="gloss-en">Kavyaaa. What day is it today?</span></div>

"Thursday. Pharmacology."

<div class="dialogue">"Ugh." Blanket over head. Blanket off. Blanket back. Then, narrowing her eyes at Meera's made bed: "She's been waking up super early lately. Kya padh rahi hai woh subah subah?"<span class="gloss-en">What is she reading so early in the morning?</span></div>

"Exams, probably."

<div class="dialogue">"Exams in September? Kaun karta hai?"<span class="gloss-en">Who does that?</span> She shrugs and shuffles out, slippers slapping stone.</div>

<<hubreturn>>
<</if>>


