:: hostel_window_view
The window of Room 304, third floor, second from the left. Below: the neem trees, the chowkidar's chair, the sign-out register on its chain. Beyond the wall, the road, the city, and   twenty minutes away   a PG in Katraj you have never heard of and a boy you have never met, who at this exact moment is staring at a ceiling fan.

<<hubreturn>>


:: manuscript_observation
<<img "swap_ritual.png" "The palm-leaf text">>
Up close: the leaves are threaded on a cord through two holes. The ink has gone brown but the characters are exact   the hand of someone dead six hundred years. Meera has pencilled a transliteration in the margin of her own notebook beside it. //Deha-vinimaya.//<span class="gloss-en">Body exchange (Sanskrit).</span> A tantric siddhi, the text says. Achievable.

Your whole training rejects it. And yet you were inside her body for three minutes tonight, so.

<<hubreturn>>


:: kavya_bathroom_mirror
A small square of mirror at chest height, clouded, rust-spotted. You get a shoulder, a collarbone gone prominent from mess food, the top curve of a breast. Enough to confirm you still exist. You don't linger. There's a queue.

<<hubreturn>>


:: morning_wash
Cold tap, the bar of soap wedged on the counter bearing the compressed fingerprints of fifty girls. Face, teeth, the Oral-B with its splayed bristles. The soap dispenser has been empty since July.

<<hubreturn>>


:: handwash_scene
You wring a salwar and two dupattas out under the tap and hang them on the line strung across the washing area. Everything in this building is slightly damp. You have stopped thinking about it.

<<hubreturn>>


:: hostel_notices
**HOSTEL NOTICE BOARD**   Mess audit Friday. Water 5:30–7:00 & 6:00–8:00 PM. Sign-out register to be filled IN INK. "Girls are reminded that guardians may visit unannounced." Someone has underlined //unannounced// three times.

<<hubreturn>>


:: corridor_water
The corridor cooler produces a thin, warm, rust-flecked stream. Sneha is ahead of you complaining about the pressure to nobody in particular. "Ek boond aayi. Ek. Main kya karun ek boond se?"<span class="gloss-en">One drop came out. One. What am I supposed to do with one drop?</span>

<<hubreturn>>


